# Vendored agent skills, held byte-identical to the upstream release that
# `tools/skills.manifest.json` records. Prettier and `check-skills` would
# otherwise be two gates that cannot both be green: the formatter rewrites a
# file, the hash stops matching, and the fix for one is the failure of the
# other. Today's release happens to satisfy this repository's Prettier config —
# the ignore is here so that the first upstream release that does not is a
# no-op rather than a deadlock. `.agents/` is the same bytes for the hosts that
# do not read `.claude/`; see the README.md in either directory.
#
# This file is the whole guard, and lefthook needs no `exclude` beside it:
# Prettier honours an ignore entry even for a path handed to it explicitly, so
# the pre-commit `prettier --write {staged_files}` leaves these alone too
# (measured — a deliberately misformatted table appended to a vendored SKILL.md
# came back byte-identical).
.claude/skills/
.agents/skills/
